  "content": {
    "title": "Duke vs Siena score: Blue Devils avoid March Madness upset to 16 seed",
    "text": "Updated March 19, 2026, 5:25 p.m. ETNo. 1 seed Duke took all it could in its NCAA first-round matchup against Siena on Thursday, March 19.The Blue Devils ultimately pulled off the 71-65 victory despite trailing by as many as 13 points to advance to the second round of the tournament on Saturday. They will play No. 9 TCU in the second round. Cam Boozer led Duke with 22 points and 13 rebounds, while his brother, Cayden Boozer added 19 points and five assists.Siena led 47-34 with 18:24 left in the game. The Blue Devils did not take their first lead of the second half until there was 3:56 left in the game.USA TODAY brought updates from the 2026 NCAA Tournament first-round matchup between the Blue Devils and Saints. Catch up here. Siena vs Duke scoreTeams1H2HFSiena432265Duke323971 Siena vs Duke highlights Siena-Duke NCAA tournament score: Blue Devils 71, Saints 65 (Final) Duke-Siena final statsStatSienaDukeScore6571Field goals25-of-65 (38%)24-of-59 (41%)3-pointers9-of-26 (35%)5-of-26 (19%)Free throws6-of-6 (100%)18-of-21 (86%)Rebounds3143Assists1511Steals53Turnovers68Points off turnovers79Blocks23Fouls1610Largest lead136 Duke avoids upset, beats Siena 71-65Duke survives the upset bid from No. 16 seed Siena, pulling out a 71-65 victory over the Saints. Siena led by 11 points at halftime and as many as 13 points in the second half. However, the Blue Devils outscored the Saints 39-22 in the second half.Siena did not have a substitution until 10 seconds left in the game and all five starters played nearly the 40 full minutes. Duke leads by 6It's about to strike midnight for the Cinderella 16-seed Siena. The Saints have gone scoreless for 6:23 of game time and trail Duke 67-61 with 1:30 left in the game.Siena is 0 for its last 7 and 1 for its last 7 from the field. It seems the Blue Devils will survive. Duke has first lead since early in first halfNo. 1 seed Duke leads Siena 63-61 following a layup by Isaiah Evans. The Blue Devils take a 7-0 run to the media timeout with 3:56 remaining. It'll be Duke basketball out of the timeout.The lead for the Blue Devils is the first since it was 10-8 with 16:11 left in the first half. Duke down by 1 vs SienaDuke has cut an 11-point halftime deficit to one point, but Siena still leads 61-60 with 5:47 left in the game. Siena has now gone on a scoring drought of 2:06 of game time.The Blue Devils have the ball and a chance to take their first lead since the 16:11 (10-8) in the first half. Duke within four of SienaEntering the under-16 timeout, Duke is on a 9-0 run and has cut the Siena lead to 47-43 with 14:51 left in the game. The Saints have misses on seven straight field goals and have no points in 3:33 of game time.The Blue Devils are outscoring Siena 11-4 in the second half. Siena goes cold, Duke mounting a comebackSiena opens the half by pushing the lead to a game-high 13 points. However, it has gone cold from the field, shooting 1-for-7. The Blue Devils have cut the lead to 47-38 with 16 minutes left in the game.Cam Boozer leads the way with 16 points for Duke, with half his points coming from free throws. Gavin Doty leads all scorers with 18 points. Second half underway between Siena-DukeThe second half is underway between Siena and Duke. The No. 16 seed holds an 11-point lead over the Blue Devils, which is the largest lead for a 16 seed over a 1 seed at halftime. Siena-Duke halftime statsStatSienaDukeScore4332Field goals17-of-31 (55%)11-of-28 (39%)3-pointers5-of-11 (45%)2-of-15 (13%)Free throws4-of-4 (100%)8-of-8 (100%)Rebounds1813Assists106Steals21Turnovers34Points off turnovers42Blocks10Fouls1310Largest lead114 Halftime: Siena 43, Duke 32How about this shocker so far? No. 16 Siena holds a double-digit lead at 43-32 over No. 1 Duke at halftime in the NCAA Tournament East Regional.The Saints are shooting 54.8% from the field in the first half and 45.5% from 3-point range. Gavin Doty has a game-high 16 points, while Francis Folefac has 13 points.Cam Boozer had 13 points on 3-of-6 shooting in the first half; the rest of the team combined for 19 points on 8-of-22 shooting (36%). Siena continues to lead Duke near end of first halfSiena holds a 35-26 lead at the final media timeout with 3:49 left in the first half over No. 1 Duke. The Blue Devils are shooting 2-of-13 (15%) from 3-point range. No. 1 Duke on upset watch?Is No. 1 Duke on upset watch? It seems so, with No. 16 seed Siena holding a 31-22 lead with 7:23 left in the first half at the under-8 media timeout.The Saints have led by as many as 11 points, with Francis Folefac leading the way with 11 points. Siena is shooting 5-of-9 from 3-point range early. Siena leads Duke early. Watch outNo. 16 Siena is giving No. 1 Duke everything it can handle early in the first round of the East Regional. The Saints hold a 22-16 lead over the Blue Devils with 11:29 left in the first half.Francis Folefac leads Siena with seven points. Cameron Boozer leads the Blue Devils with seven points.What time is Siena vs Duke First Round game?No. 1 Duke vs No. 16 Siena tips off at 2:50 PM (EST) on Thursday, March 19 from Bon Secours Wellness Arena (Greenville, South Carolina).What channel is Siena vs Duke First Round game?No. 1 Duke vs No. 16 Siena is airing live on CBS.How to stream Siena vs Duke First Round gameNo. 1 Duke vs No. 16 Siena is available to stream on Fubo.Watch the NCAA Tournament all March long with FuboMen's March Madness schedule todaySee the schedule, live scores and results for all of Thursday's NCAA Tournament action here.2026 March Madness datesMarch 17-18: First FourMarch 19-20: First RoundMarch 21-22: Second RoundMarch 26-27: Sweet 16March 28-29: Elite 8April 4: Final FourApril 6: National Championship",
